  "owner_review": "Integration approved the bounded kernel/SDK contract and coordinated the VM. Filesystem reviewed copyout, descriptor ownership and metadata. Existing shared syscall slots and experimental admission gates are unchanged.",
  "runtime_scope": {
    "addressing": "Unnamed AF_UNIX pairs. Standalone SOCK_SEQPACKET socket creation and half-close are outside the supported pair scope.",
    "wire": "4096-byte records, up to four SCM_RIGHTS attachments, zero-length records without rights, and a bounded duplex queue.",
    "checks": "Scalar, vector and sendmsg calls preserve records. MSG_TRUNC discards one tail, PEEK leaves data and rights queued, and a failed destination check permits an intact retry. Send backpressure and oversize rejection publish no prefix. Rights stay live after sender close, and transferred packet endpoints retain identity. Flags, poll, socket stat, close/EOF, legacy rights-call refusal and stream controls passed.",
